---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/alternatives/attentive-alternative';
const title = 'Attentive Alternatives for Shopify (2026)';
const desc = 'Compare Attentive alternatives by merchant job, channel eligibility, matched costs and migration readiness, including retired Yotpo entries.';
const alternatives = [
  { slug: 'postscript', name: 'Postscript', job: 'SMS drop operations', text: 'Evaluate a mechanical-keyboard drop: opt-in capture, replies, launch scheduling and purchase exits. Postscript publishes plan and usage pricing, including a Starter minimum spend and carrier fees. Compare your actual quote rather than assuming an enterprise-free or cheaper replacement.', source: 'https://postscript.io/pricing' },
  { slug: 'sequenzy', name: 'Sequenzy', job: 'Email lifecycle ownership', text: 'Test a specialty-tea replenishment email using the required Shopify purchase events. The pricing page lists a Shopify integration; confirm event coverage, historical sync and plan limits in your account. An email evaluation does not establish SMS replacement coverage. Keep an existing SMS provider only if that channel remains useful and shared suppression can be operated reliably.', source: 'https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing' },
  { slug: 'omnisend', name: 'Omnisend', job: 'Coordinated email and SMS', text: 'Test an artisan-coffee restock across email and SMS, including caps and channel-specific permission. Current documentation distinguishes newer and legacy plan rules: accounts starting paid plans on or after May 4, 2026 need Pro to purchase an SMS Credits Subscription. Confirm your account rules, enabled countries, sender setup and separate SMS charges.', source: 'https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/3533018-omnisend-pricing-plans-2026' },
  { slug: 'klaviyo', name: 'Klaviyo', job: 'Purchase-aware cross-channel journeys', text: 'For climbing-gear winback, test Shopify identity mapping, a new purchase exit and SMS fallback rules. SMS consent collection and sending are limited to supported countries. Number types, registration and account eligibility vary; validate the required sender before treating consolidation as feasible.', source: 'https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4402914866843' },
  { slug: 'smsbump', name: 'SMSBump / Yotpo SMS', job: 'Retired-product warning', text: 'Keep this historical identity distinct from an available replacement. The Yotpo SMS lifecycle notice says the application is decommissioned and its dashboard and background services are inactive. Do not plan a new Attentive migration into it; ask Yotpo support about unresolved historical records.', source: 'https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/' },
  { slug: 'recart', name: 'Recart', job: 'SMS acquisition and recovery', text: 'For a board-game allocation release, test list capture and cart recovery without messaging customers who already bought or exhausted their allocation. Recart presents a broader Shopify SMS and list-growth service, not merely a recovery-only tool. Confirm your markets, sender, support scope and quote; savings are not established by this exercise.', source: 'https://recart.com/' },
  { slug: 'sendlane', name: 'Sendlane', job: 'Owner-led email and SMS consolidation', text: 'For a pottery studio, ask the operator to rebuild welcome and post-purchase messages with the required Shopify events. Sendlane lists Shopify integration and email/SMS offerings. Confirm paid-account SMS eligibility, countries, sender provisioning and which migration tasks support will actually perform before agreeing a cutover.', source: 'https://www.sendlane.com/pricing' },
  { slug: 'yotpo-email-sms', name: 'Yotpo Email & SMS', job: 'Historical suite reference', text: 'Yotpo announced full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Existing reviews and loyalty relationships do not make this retired messaging product a new consolidation option. Inventory surviving integrations and obtain a supported messaging destination instead.', source: 'https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/' },
];
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Why consider an Attentive alternative?', answer: 'Compare actual costs, required markets, services and operator workload. A smaller store is not automatically a poor fit, and a larger store does not automatically need Attentive.' },
  { question: 'Is leaving Attentive a downgrade?', answer: 'No general ranking follows from a switch. Evaluate the merchant job and account eligibility; a move may consolidate channels, change support needs or retain a specialist.' },
  { question: 'Does Attentive have a universal enterprise minimum?', answer: 'Its pricing page describes tailored pricing by message volume, subscriber list size, channels and selected AI products. Use your quote and contract; this guide establishes no universal minimum.' },
  { question: 'Must I split email and SMS?', answer: 'No. Attentive offers both channels, and consolidation candidates also exist. A split requires an explicit owner for identity, permission and cross-channel send coordination.' },
  { question: 'Can I move to SMSBump or Yotpo Email & SMS?', answer: 'These are retained historical entries, not current migration recommendations. Yotpo announced Email and SMS deprecation, and its SMS application now has a decommissioned notice.' },
  { question: 'Can SMS consent move with the list?', answer: 'Do not treat a phone number or email opt-in as SMS permission. Review available evidence, current suppressions, purpose, destination requirements and country-specific rules before importing or activating.' },
  { question: 'How long does an Attentive migration take?', answer: 'There is no fixed duration here. Contract notice, export access, sender provisioning, integration testing and staff readiness determine the schedule. A published vendor migration offer is not a guarantee for your account.' },
  { question: 'When should I stay on Attentive?', answer: 'Consider staying when verified channel coverage, services, workflow control and matched costs meet your needs. Test an internal edit and purchase exit before attributing operational friction to the platform.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container max-w-4xl">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/alternatives">Alternatives</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span>Attentive alternatives</span></nav>
      <header>
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Shopify messaging decisions</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Attentive alternatives for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Choose around the journeys you need to run, rather than a presumed enterprise-to-SMB downshift. Attentive offers SMS and email; leaving does not inherently require two tools or produce savings.</p>
        <p class="mt-5">The eight original entries below are organized by job, not ranked. Two are retired Yotpo messaging identities. Merchant exercises are proposed tests, not customer results.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-12">
        <TldrBox title="Conditional shortlist" picks={[
          { label: 'SMS operations', tool: 'Postscript', reason: 'Test drop workflows against the actual plan and sender requirements.' },
          { label: 'Email lifecycle', tool: 'Sequenzy', reason: 'Verify Shopify events for replenishment before adopting.' },
          { label: 'Channel coordination', tool: 'Omnisend or Klaviyo', reason: 'Check account eligibility, countries and purchase exits.' },
        ]} />
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14">
        <h2>Compare the work, then the platform</h2>
        <p>For a vinyl label, test whether an internal owner can edit a release message, apply VIP eligibility and stop sends after purchase. For an outdoor brand, verify country coverage and required creative services. These may support staying on Attentive as readily as leaving.</p>
        <p>A mechanical-keyboard shop can test SMS specialization; a tea seller can test replenishment email. Neither requires Sequenzy plus Postscript by default. If you retain separate tools, assign responsibility for conflicts, identity updates and opt-outs before running both.</p>
        <p><a class="link" href="https://www.attentive.com/pricing">Attentive pricing</a> is tailored to volume, list size, channels and AI products. Do not substitute an invented monthly floor or order-count threshold for a quote. Likewise, a vendor reporting attributed revenue does not establish incremental profit.</p>
        <h2>One matched cost worksheet</h2>
        <p><strong>Cost comparison:</strong> Use the same quarter, reachable contacts, email sends, SMS segments/MMS, countries, sender types and required features for each quote. Recurring cost equals platform charges plus usage, carrier and sender charges, required services and staff hours at the same hourly rate, less included credits counted once. Record migration labor, provisioning, overlap and remaining contract obligations separately as transition costs. Compare like currencies and tax treatment. Assess incremental contribution with a comparable holdout where practical; revenue minus fees is not TCO.</p>
      </article>
      <section class="space-y-8 py-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Options by merchant job</h2>
        {alternatives.map((option) => (
          <section class="card" id={option.slug}>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black">{option.name}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 font-bold">{option.job}</p>
            <p class="mt-4">{option.text}</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm"><a class="link" href={option.source}>Vendor documentation</a> · <a class="link" href={`/apps/${option.slug}`}>Local {option.name} review</a></p>
          </section>
        ))}
      </section>
      <article class="prose-shopify">
        <h2>Migration gates, without a fixed deadline</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Confirm exit and access.</strong> Review notice, renewal, exports and record retention with the contract owner. Inventory keywords, forms, sender numbers, scheduled campaigns, automations and integrations. Ask both vendors which senders can port and what provisioning remains.</li>
          <li><strong>Reconcile identity and permission.</strong> Map Shopify customer IDs, normalized email/phone identifiers and event IDs. Do not merge shared phone numbers blindly. Preserve available timestamp, source, disclosure, purpose and country evidence. Keep email and SMS permission distinct; apply current opt-outs and exclusions before activation.</li>
          <li><strong>Test meaningful exits.</strong> Use controlled recipients to test cart-to-order transitions, purchases made during a delay, opt-outs and frequency caps. A board-game allocation purchase must retire its recovery message; a tea subscription purchase must change replenishment eligibility. Verify actual integration events rather than assuming every historical event replays.</li>
          <li><strong>Retire queues deliberately.</strong> Assign one active owner per journey. Disable old triggers, scheduled campaigns and pending queues; confirm cancellation behavior with support. Deduplicate retries and replayed events using stable event/journey identifiers. Recheck permission and purchase state at dispatch where supported; quarantine uncertain events rather than replaying them broadly.</li>
          <li><strong>Cut over only when ready.</strong> Validate sender approval, test delivery and internal edit access. Monitor failures and duplicate-send reports. For rollback, pause the new system, reconcile already-sent IDs and current suppressions, then resume only one verified path. Never reactivate an old queue wholesale.</li>
          <li><strong>Hand off support and ownership.</strong> Give support the active sender, reply/opt-out behavior, unresolved imports and escalation contacts. Give finance the worksheet and operations the journey register. Retain required records before account closure; confirm export access ends when expected.</li>
        </ol>
        <h2>What counts as evidence</h2>
        <p>Record the internal owner’s time and support dependencies for a climbing-gear flash-sale edit. For a vinyl drop, record permission failures and purchase exits alongside incremental contribution. Define the review window before testing. No fixed savings percentage, preserved recovery rate or migration duration is established here.</p>
        <p>Checked November 25, 2026. Account-specific terms and sender availability still require confirmation. See <a class="link" href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/2747083-get-started-with-sms-channel">Omnisend channel setup</a> and <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4404274419355">Klaviyo SMS setup</a> for configuration dependencies.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="py-8 text-sm">
        <p class="font-black">Related guides</p>
        <p><a class="link" href="/apps/attentive">Attentive review</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> · <a class="link" href="/alternatives/postscript-alternative">Postscript alternatives</a> · <a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Attentive alternatives FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
